course: dictionary
lesson: 6815
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Orthodox can mean the usual, accepted way of doing something. «An orthodox method» is the normal way to do a job. Its opposite is unorthodox, which means unusual or different from what most people do.
explain: Orthodox also has a special meaning in religion. The Orthodox Church is a big family of Christian churches, strong in Greece, Russia, Ukraine and Serbia. Orthodox Jews keep Jewish laws very strictly, such as the rules for the sabbath and for food.
explain: The sentence around a word tells you which meaning is right. Look for clues like church, religion, Christians or Jews, and for words like method or way of doing something. Then test your meaning: does it still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Orthodox means following the usual, accepted ways of doing something.
fact: Unorthodox means unusual, not the usual way.
fact: The Orthodox Church is a big family of Christian churches, with icons, candles and ancient services.
fact: «Christmas is on 25 December, but many Orthodox churches celebrate it on 7 January» because they use an older calendar.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so check the clues around it before you decide.
exercise: Mia tries an unorthodox way to tidy her room: she rolls everything into one big ball. What does unorthodox mean? | The usual, accepted way | *Unusual, not the usual way | Very messy | Very quick
exercise: «Christmas is on 25 December, but many Orthodox churches celebrate it on 7 January.» Why do some Orthodox churches celebrate on 7 January? | Christmas is on a different day for everyone | They forgot the date | They do not celebrate Christmas at all | *They use an older calendar
exercise: «In the Ukrainian Orthodox Church, a panakhyda is a prayer service for someone who has died.» What is a panakhyda? | A type of Orthodox Jewish food | A church bell | A kind of Easter bread | *A prayer service for someone who has died
test: «Orthodox Jews keep the Jewish laws strictly.» Which is one example of a law they keep? | *The sabbath rest | Making priests from women | Easter on a different day | Christmas on 7 January
test: «Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain only men.» What does ordain mean here? | *Make into priests | Lose a job | Paint a picture of | Sing loudly
exam: Which is an orthodox way to do a school project? | Ask the dog to do it | Make it up as you go | Build it out of ice | *Follow the usual, accepted steps your teacher shows you
